   "notes": [
    "In boost mode (VO at its normal 10 V) the converter draws current pulses near 0.8 A, so series resistance matters: for full load at VDD = 2 V the inductor DC resistance plus the wiring from battery to inductor and inductor to LX should total no more than 0.3 Ω, the battery's own internal resistance no more than 0.5 Ω, and a low-ESR capacitor of at least 10 µF should sit across the battery to average the current over each cycle.",
    "Where a test condition names a VO value, VO is driven from outside with the inductor removed and the boost converter stopped.",
    "Limits are fully tested at +25°C only; guard-banded test limits, set from temperature characterization, cover the temperature extremes.",
    "Note 4: IIT is the largest input current that still asserts neither a logic high nor a logic low."
   ]
