   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical application",
   "page": 1,
   "description": "A battery of 2 V to 5 V feeds VDD, with C1 across it. L1 runs from the supply to LX and Schottky D1 from LX to VO, where C3 holds the boosted rail near 10 V. HORNB and HORNS, complementary outputs, drive the brass and silver electrodes of a three-terminal piezo horn. The horn's feedback electrode returns to FEED through R2; R1 runs from FEED to HORNB and C4 from FEED to HORNS. HRNEN is the enable line: tri-state, low or high on the RE46C317, low or high on the RE46C318.",
